          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765232069008_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Input: `{{$context.$nodes.INVOKE_ACTION_WF_AGENT.$output.output}}`\n\"You are generating an information display for an Agentic App. The action result will conform to one of two possible JSON schemas. Based on which schema is present, output exactly one escaped <oraInfoDisplay> element (no additional text, explanation, or markdown). Follow these instructions precisely:\n\n1) If the result matches the Schema (has 'message' and 'event_name'):\nOutput a single escaped <oraInfoDisplay> with key 'unique:registration{event_name}'.\nUse patternId 'cardWidget'.\nThe JSON payload properties must include:\ntitle: set to the event_name\npatternId: 'cardWidget'\ndescription: a one-line summary (use the 'message' value)\nproperties: an object matching the cardWidget schema:\nsubject: event_name\ntimestamp: Just now,\nbadgeText: SUCCESS,\nsummary: message\nvariant: 'info'\nExample output shape:\n<oraInfoDisplay key=\"unique:registration{eventname}\">\n{ \"title\": \"...\", \"patternId\":\"cardWidget\", \"description\":\"...\", \"properties\": { \"subject\":\"...\", \"summary\":\"...\", \"variant\":\"info\" } }\n</oraInfoDisplay>\n\n2) If the result matches the Event Schema (event_name, start_date, end_date, registrants, event_format, description, event_team, optionally meeting_link and meeting_details):\nOutput a single escaped <oraInfoDisplay> with key 'unique:event{eventname}'.\nUse patternId 'recordWidget'.\nMap the event fields into the recordWidget fields array. Use readOnly: true for display-only behavior unless the app requires editing.\nUse the following field mappings (field id, type, label, value):\nid: 'event_name', type: 'text', label: 'Event Name', value: eventname\nid: 'start_date', type: 'text', label: 'Start Date and Time', value: startdate\nid: 'end_date', type: 'text', label: 'End Date and Time', value: enddate\nid: 'registrants', type: 'text', label: 'Registrants', value: registrants\nid: 'event_format', type: 'text', label: 'Format', value: eventformat\nid: 'event_team', type: 'text', label: 'Event Team', value: eventteam\nid: 'meeting_link', type: 'text', label: 'Meeting Link', value: meetinglink (include only if present)\nid: 'meeting_details', type: 'textarea', label: 'Meeting Details', value: meetingdetails (include only if present)\nid: 'description', type: 'textarea', label: 'Description', value: description\nEnsure the recordWidget JSON follows the recordWidget schema: include id (use 'event_details{event_name}') and readOnly: true (or false if editable).\nExample output shape:\n<oraInfoDisplay key=\"unique:event{eventname}\">\n{\n\"title\":\"Event: {event_name}\",\n\"patternId\":\"recordWidget\",\n\"description\":\"Event details\",\n\"properties\": {\n\"id\":\"eventdetails{event_name}\",\n\"readOnly\": true,\n\"fields\":[ { \"id\":\"event_name\", \"type\":\"text\", \"label\":\"Event Name\", \"value\":\"...\" }, ... ]\n}\n}\n</oraInfoDisplay>\n\n4) General rules:\nOutput only one escaped <oraInfoDisplay> element (no surrounding text).\nUse the widget patternIds exactly: 'cardWidget', 'recordWidget', or 'multiRecordWidget'.\nFor recordWidget date/time fields we store the full ISO datetime string in a text or textarea field to preserve time zone info.\nFor recordWidget textarea field types, do not moit or trim the content. display full text \nKeep titles concise and descriptions short.\nDo not fabricate missing recipient or linking data. Omit optional fields if they are not present in the input.\nDo not include any XML that is not the single escaped <oraInfoDisplay> element.\"\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\nERROR HANDLING\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\nIf the output {{$context.$nodes.INVOKE_ACTION_WF_AGENT.$output.output}} has no data or contains the text \"Error occurred on this action\". Return the below as plain text\n\nThe action could not be completed. Please try again."
            }
