          "id": "1765226050287",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765226050288_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are given this data {{$context.$nodes.GET_UPCOMING_REGISTERED_EVENT_ALERT.$output.output}}. If it is not an empty object produce one communication suggestions with below details.\n\n###email###\n1.Using the contents in {{$context.$nodes.GET_UPCOMING_REGISTERED_EVENT_ALERT.$output.output}} create an \"email\" communication suggestion with the following:\ntitle: Share Event Details\nsubject: A one line description about the event\ncontent: Using first person tone, generate the email content mentioning why you think event is useful. Also mention the relevant event details as well. At the end add a new line and signature with name as {{$context.$app.$OraUserContext.fullName}}. Format the content in html rich text.\n\n### Time Zone Formatting Rule\nFor `items[].Subtitle`, display `StartDate - EndDate` but convert any time zone into a **standard short abbreviation**.\n\n- If the time zone is an **IANA zone** (e.g., `America/Los_Angeles`, `Asia/Kolkata`, `Europe/London`), convert it to the **correct local abbreviation for that date**, accounting for daylight saving time (e.g., `PST/PDT`, `CST/CDT`, `GMT/BST`, `IST`).\n- If the time zone is already an abbreviation (e.g., `PST`, `IST`, `JST`), keep it unchanged.\n- If the time zone cannot be resolved, fall back to a numeric UTC offset if available.\n- Do **not** modify the date or time values — only replace the time zone label.\n\nIf the data given to you is empty. Only return {} and nothing else"
            }
